  wall clock 17s

  What this run proves: the three components build for wasm32-wasip2, their own
  test suites pass, the shared core has not drifted, and each component behaves
  correctly end to end against a live https endpoint, including refusing what it
  should refuse before it touches the network.
  What it does not prove: stage 3 data is a local fake, so no on-chain state is
  involved and nothing here was signed, broadcast or paid. Mainnet evidence lives
  in stage 4 and in demo/artifacts/mainnet-readpath/.

  RESULT: green, 17s, every number above came from this run.
